Q2 — Feature claims and ablations

We appreciate this observation and clarify the practical meaning of these feature gains as follows.

Marginal does not mean negligible. While the degradation from removing physical alignment is smaller than that from removing CERRA or NFL, it is consistently positive across all three farms, both horizons, and both metrics—12 out of 12 settings show improvement when alignment is included. This consistency across diverse farm configurations (6, 14, and 21 turbines) is strong evidence that the component captures a genuine physical signal rather than fitting noise.
Small gains compound in practice. In operational wind power forecasting, even a fraction of a percentage point in MAE translates to meaningful economic value in dispatch and reserve scheduling over thousands of hours. The alignment component achieves this gain at zero learnable parameter cost, as it is a non-parametric deterministic transformation.
