Reviewer py3A

We thank the reviewer for the constructive feedback. We have addressed each point carefully in the following.

W1 & Q1 — Methodological novelty

Thanks for the comment. We would like to clarify our technical contributions as follows:

Our key insight is identifying why existing methods fail at wind power forecasting with NWP: data heterogeneity between point-based SCADA and grid-based NWP, and the directional physical interactions governing power conversion. Designing a framework that systematically addresses both challenges through geometric encoding and spectral fusion is itself a non-trivial contribution.
The geometric encoder deliberately avoids learned parameters because the underlying physics (cosine yaw-misalignment law, divergence, vorticity) is known and exact. We use domain knowledge directly, as a design choice, which is consistent with the broader trend toward physics-informed ML, where injecting known structure improves generalization.
Table 3 shows that simply giving existing models access to the same SCADA+NWP inputs via standard fusion yields weaker results than our framework. This demonstrates that our specific integration of geometric priors with Fourier-domain fusion is not an obvious assembly.
